<!-- LFG Forever's key binding: "Open LFG Forever", which opens or closes the
     window like /lfg.

     NOT listed in LFGForever.toc: the client loads a file named Bindings.xml
     from the addon's root by itself, and listing it as well registers the
     binding twice. No Blizzard TOC lists its own Bindings.xml.

     * name is the action, saved with the player's keys: renaming it unbinds
       every player.
     * category groups the row on Blizzard's Keybindings page; the page titles
       the section with _G[category] (Keybindings.lua:220-226). The global, and
       the row's label BINDING_NAME_LFGFOREVER_TOGGLE, are set in core/slash.lua.
     * No default key, by the author's decision: nothing can clash.
     * The body runs in the global environment on the key press, so it calls a
       global, also in core/slash.lua.

     .claude/rules/keybinding.md -->
<Bindings>
	<Binding name="LFGFOREVER_TOGGLE" category="BINDING_HEADER_LFGFOREVER">
		LFGForever_ToggleWindow()
	</Binding>
</Bindings>
